  "scope": "The NPC classes and listeners listed in `unchanged` compiled unchanged on JDK 11 with Kotlin 1.8.20 and the published ConstLib 1.4.28 (NPCs, Items and Scenery values checked against the suffixes of the names used), with the unchanged OptionHandler, Plugin, IntType, core.api.Container and Direction. Original text inserted into adapters at generation time: NPC.create (both overloads), the Skills ids, BankBoothListener.BANK_BOOTHS, the BarcrawlType constants with their NPC ids and BarcrawlType.forId. Everything else is a recording adapter answering from the case: the NPC constructor and the NPC/Entity members the classes reach (init, tick, handleTickActions, finalizeDeath, onAttack, onImpact, getSwingHandler, walks, aggression, direction, transform, attributes, chat), Location (the constructor plane and 15-bit packing of Location.kt, its transforms and withinDistance), the InteractionListeners registry (on/setDest recorded in order), NPCDefinition handlers and option handlers, the dialogue interpreter and DialogueLabeller.open, ContentAPI, the combat pulse, swing handlers, skills, quests, diaries, ground items, spells, the zone monitor, DeathTask, random functions, the random event and holiday NPC lookups, the barcrawl manager and the gnome cooking completion dialogue. The clock the original reads itself (IdleAbstractNPC) is recorded relative to it in whole seconds.",
